\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{An algebraic reflection form}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Let #{k} be a field with involution #{z\mapsto\bar z}.
Its fixed field #{k_0} is ordered, and suppose
#{|z|^2:=\bar z z\ge0} for every #{z\in k}.
An ordered field with the identity involution and
#{\mathbb C} with fixed field #{\mathbb R} are the two
basic cases. Let #{\mathscr A} be a finite-dimensional
unital #{k}-algebra. An \newvocab{algebraic anti-reflection}
is a conjugate-linear map #{\Theta:\mathscr A\to\mathscr A}
such that
##{\Theta(1)=1,\qquad
 \Theta(ab)=\Theta(b)\Theta(a),\qquad
 \Theta^2=\bbI_{\mathscr A}.}
Choose a unital subalgebra #{\mathscr A_+}, called the
\newvocab{positive half-algebra}. Its choice is part of the data.}

\p{A #{k}-linear functional #{\ell:\mathscr A\to k} is
\newvocab{reflection compatible} if
##{\ell(\Theta a)=\overline{\ell(a)}\qquad(a\in\mathscr A).}
Its \newvocab{reflection form} on #{\mathscr A_+} is
##{B_\ell(a,b)=\ell((\Theta a)b).}
The functional is \newvocab{reflection positive on the half-algebra}
if #{B_\ell(a,a)\in k_0} and #{B_\ell(a,a)\ge0} for every
#{a\in\mathscr A_+}. The same condition can be imposed on a
specified linear subspace, such as its even gauge-invariant part.
Normalization means #{\ell(1)=1}; it is a separate condition.}

\p{The commutative function-algebra case has the scalar
\vocabk{reflection convention}{fdip-007M}. The order-reversing rule
also accommodates the paired generators of the
\vocabk{ring paired coefficient}{fdip-00TJ}.}
